## Appendix B: Proof of Theorem A (Adaptation Advantage)

**Theorem A.** Define
\[
U_{\text{adapt}} = \mathbb{E}_{t \sim P_T} \left[ \max_{\theta \in \Theta} U(\theta, t) \right]
\]
and
\[
U_{\text{fix}} = \max_{\theta \in \Theta} \mathbb{E}_{t \sim P_T} \left[ U(\theta, t) \right].
\]
Then
\[
\Delta U_{\text{adapt}} = U_{\text{adapt}} - U_{\text{fix}} \geq 0
\]
with equality if and only if there exists a single configuration \(\theta^*\) that is optimal for all tasks with positive probability.

**Proof.** For any fixed \(\theta' \in \Theta\), we have
\[
\max_{\theta \in \Theta} U(\theta, t) \geq U(\theta', t) \quad \forall t.
\]
Taking expectations over \(t \sim P_T\):
\[
\mathbb{E}_t \left[ \max_{\theta \in \Theta} U(\theta, t) \right] \geq \mathbb{E}_t \left[ U(\theta', t) \right].
\]
Since this holds for all \(\theta'\), it holds in particular for
\[
\theta^* = \arg\max_{\theta \in \Theta} \mathbb{E}_t \left[ U(\theta, t) \right].
\]
Thus
\[
U_{\text{adapt}} \geq \mathbb{E}_t \left[ U(\theta^*, t) \right] = U_{\text{fix}},
\]
so \(\Delta U_{\text{adapt}} \geq 0\).

For strict inequality, suppose there exist two tasks \(t_a, t_b\) with \(P(t_a) > 0\), \(P(t_b) > 0\), and two configurations \(\theta_a, \theta_b\) such that
\[
U(\theta_a, t_a) - U(\theta_b, t_a) \geq \delta_a > 0,
\]
\[
U(\theta_b, t_b) - U(\theta_a, t_b) \geq \delta_b > 0.
\]
Assume no single configuration \(\theta\) achieves \(\max_{\theta'} U(\theta', t)\) for both \(t_a\) and \(t_b\). Then for any fixed \(\theta\), there is a positive probability task on which it incurs a strictly positive regret. Hence
\[
\mathbb{E}_t \left[ \max_{\theta} U(\theta, t) \right] - \mathbb{E}_t \left[ U(\theta, t) \right] > 0
\]
for every \(\theta\), which implies
\[
U_{\text{adapt}} - U_{\text{fix}} > 0.
\]
Conversely, if there exists \(\theta^*\) that is optimal for all \(t\) with positive probability, then
\[
U(\theta^*, t) = \max_{\theta} U(\theta, t) \quad \forall t \text{ with } P(t) > 0,
\]
so \(U_{\text{adapt}} = U_{\text{fix}}\) and \(\Delta U_{\text{adapt}} = 0\). \(\square\)

**Corollary (Regret Interpretation).** Define the regret of configuration \(\theta\) for task \(t\):
\[
R(\theta, t) = U^*(t) - U(\theta, t), \quad U^*(t) = \max_{\theta'} U(\theta', t).
\]
Then
\[
R_{\text{fix}} = \min_{\theta} \mathbb{E}_{t \sim P_T} [R(\theta, t)].
\]
Since
\[
\mathbb{E}_t [R(\theta, t)] = \mathbb{E}_t [U^*(t)] - \mathbb{E}_t [U(\theta, t)] = U_{\text{adapt}} - \mathbb{E}_t [U(\theta, t)],
\]
minimizing over \(\theta\) gives
\[
R_{\text{fix}} = U_{\text{adapt}} - \max_{\theta} \mathbb{E}_t [U(\theta, t)] = U_{\text{adapt}} - U_{\text{fix}} = \Delta U_{\text{adapt}}.
\]
Thus the adaptation advantage equals the minimum expected regret of a fixed configuration.

