## Appendix H: Hardware Heterogeneity and Structural Diversity

Let \(Q = [q_{ir}]\) be the capability matrix, where \(q_{ir}\) is the capability of node \(i\) for role \(r\).

**Coefficient of variation.** For each role \(r\), define
\[
\mu_r = \frac{1}{|V|} \sum_{i \in V} q_{ir}, \quad \sigma_r = \sqrt{\frac{1}{|V|} \sum_{i \in V} (q_{ir} - \mu_r)^2}.
\]
Then
\[
H_{\text{hardware}} = \frac{1}{|\mathcal{R}|} \sum_{r \in \mathcal{R}} \frac{\sigma_r}{\mu_r + \epsilon}.
\]
This measures the average dispersion of capabilities across nodes.

**Structural diversity.** Let \(\mathbf{q}_i = (q_{i1}, \dots, q_{i|\mathcal{R}|})\) be the capability vector of node \(i\). Define the pairwise correlation between nodes \(i\) and \(j\) as
\[
\rho_{ij} = \frac{\sum_{r} (q_{ir} - \mu_r)(q_{jr} - \mu_r)}{\sqrt{\sum_{r} (q_{ir} - \mu_r)^2} \sqrt{\sum_{r} (q_{jr} - \mu_r)^2}}.
\]
Then
\[
H_{\text{corr}}(Q) = 1 - \frac{2}{|V|(|V|-1)} \sum_{i < j} \rho_{ij}.
\]
This measures diversity of capability profiles: if all nodes have identical profiles, \(\rho_{ij} = 1\) for all \(i,j\) and \(H_{\text{corr}} = 0\); if profiles are uncorrelated, \(H_{\text{corr}} \approx 1\). The full heterogeneity measure is
\[
H_{\text{hardware}}^{\text{full}} = H_{\text{hardware}} + \kappa H_{\text{corr}}(Q),
\]
where \(\kappa\) is a weighting parameter.

